    s("Lean mass and health",
      "Higher lean mass, particularly muscle, is linked with better blood sugar control, stronger bones, better balance and longer life. Low lean mass in older adults predicts frailty, falls and hospital stays. Keeping lean mass through midlife and later is one of the most valuable things a training plan can do.",
      "Lean mass is not the only marker of health. Body fat distribution, fitness, blood pressure and blood markers matter too. A doctor can assess these if you have concerns about your health."),
