    s("Using the estimate with clients",
      "For a new client, the Lee estimate gives a quick starting figure to discuss alongside weight, waist and strength. It is useful for explaining why muscle matters, how it changes with age and why the plan includes resistance training. It should not be used to judge whether a client has gained muscle over a few months.",
      "When discussing the number, explain the ethnicity simplification and the population nature of the estimate. For a client who trains, it will likely underestimate their muscle. For a client who is inactive with higher body fat, it may overestimate it. Use their training log and measurements to track real change."),
